01:12:18.400 --> 01:12:47.994
I think it is different That a various interpretation which is marked based on the theories of others The Hikalaam versus the Yahyaani Samadhi Shri It not I believe that Kevah in Alay has to do with psychology What is more important for me I have two agendas

01:12:47.994 --> 01:12:59.994
Alright? It's not a question of just putting more hours. Because you could put more hours and while you're studying Torah, your mind is wandering around a thousand things.

01:12:59.994 --> 01:13:07.994
You're not putting any energy, you're not concentrating on this. Doesn't mean that you got... that's not Keva.

01:13:07.994 --> 01:13:28.994
The Keva is a mental attitude. What is the more important thing for you? So therefore a person could be working in theory eight hours a day, six hours a day, and studying six hours a day, or whatever it is, and for him the Torah is Keva.

01:13:28.994 --> 01:13:36.994
For the other person, no, in the same situation, the Merakha is Keva. He's more concentrated on this, he's got more energies on this, and so on.

01:13:36.994 --> 01:13:47.994
So, Ayin is then Geva and not Keen Arai. And the question is your mental and psychological energies and attitude.

01:13:47.994 --> 01:13:50.994
That is what makes the difference between one and the other.

01:13:50.994 --> 01:13:55.994
It's not just a question of hours. It's the way you focus. That's very good.

01:13:55.994 --> 01:13:59.994
It's not a question of because you could have people studying the whole day and they're not studying the whole day.

01:13:59.994 --> 01:14:03.994
The mind is wandering. Or maybe they cannot absorb it.

01:14:03.994 --> 01:14:09.234
Maybe they have some problems, economic problems, social problems, family problems, I don't know about that.

01:14:09.234 --> 01:14:12.434
They're not doing, they're not Tora Tami, it's not Keva.

01:14:12.434 --> 01:14:17.554
And therefore, it's Arbe'asu b'al Bishamu Bar Yochai, Bero Hatami Adan.

01:14:17.554 --> 01:14:21.594
You know? And this is not Tora Tami Keva.

01:14:21.594 --> 01:14:26.714
You see? On the other hand, the other person who studies three hours with a clear mind,

01:14:26.714 --> 01:14:31.594
this is really what he believes in, and now all this energy, maybe that's Tora Keva.

01:14:31.594 --> 01:14:38.594
That's my point. So the Hakhamim, they didn't distinguish, I mean they say more hours or less hours.

01:14:38.594 --> 01:14:47.594
That's why Hosef Tora Tov, who is the man, Ezer Sha'od, Yoter Zeman, they say Yoter Zeman, or Keva, Tavaq Qabua, and Tavaq Araf.

01:14:47.594 --> 01:15:04.988
Question of priorities What is the most important What is your more important goal To have another million dollars or to study another masakka That the question What is Bera

01:15:04.988 --> 01:15:14.988
Now, if you make a phone call to your broker or play with your computer in Kamalati, it doesn't mean you shouldn't make it.

01:15:14.988 --> 01:15:18.988
But this question is what is more important to you.

01:15:18.988 --> 01:15:33.988
And that is the beautiful Gemara. So Laduna is in Loa, Degani, Deganeja, yes, Degamushef Adarai, Zeripiha, Yasalta Deganeja, what you do, all these things.

01:15:33.988 --> 01:15:45.988
So I believe that all those contradictions are great because they create a tension and they force the individuals to resolve this forking path, you know, crossroads that you have to make a decision.

01:15:45.988 --> 01:15:49.988
And there are close ones in your life. You will get a decision.

01:15:51.988 --> 01:15:54.988
